  <section class="section-content" id="key-features-tw">
    <div class="il-container">
      <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What Are the Key Features of Two-Wheeler Insurance?</h2>
      
      <div class="flex-div mt-40 read-more-list">
        <div class="list-block org-list width-equal org-list-block">
          <ul>
            <li>
              <h4 class="heading4">Coverage Against Own Damages </h4>
              <p class="text">The best bike insurance offers a financial cushion in the event your bike suffers damages from accidents, fire, theft, natural disasters, etc. This ensures you are not burdened with heavy out-of-pocket expenses after an unfortunate incident.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h4 class="heading4">Coverage Against Third-party Liabilities </h4>
              <p class="text">Bike insurance offers financial protection against damages or injuries caused to third parties in an accident where you and your bike are at fault. Third-party coverage is also mandatory by Indian law.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h4 class="heading4">Policy Customisation</h4>
              <p class="text">You can fortify the base policy's coverage with the help of add-ons. Common bike insurance add-on covers include engine protection, zero depreciation, roadside assistance, etc. Choose add-ons depending on your riding habits and risk exposure.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="more-list-show">
              <h4 class="heading4">Personal Accident Cover </h4>
              <p class="text">Get financial support when you, the owner-rider, suffer an accidental injury while riding your bike. With personal accident cover, your nominee gets a payout in case of your accidental death.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="list-block org-list width-equal org-list-block">
          <ul>
            <li class="more-list-show">
              <h4 class="heading4">Online Buying/Renewal Process </h4>
              <p class="text">You can easily compare bike insurance plans online, calculate premiums and get covered instantly without any paperwork. You can also renew your bike insurance policy via your insurer’s website or app.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="more-list-show">
              <h4 class="heading4">No Claim Bonus </h4>
              <p class="text">Insurance companies reward you with a discount in premiums for every claim-free year. The NCB discount can go up to 50%. You can claim this discount at the time of your bike insurance policy renewal.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="more-list-show">
              <h4 class="heading4">Cashless Repairs </h4>
              <p class="text">You get access to authorised garages where you can repair your damaged bike without making any upfront payments. Just raise a claim and the insurer directly settles the repair bills – you just have to pay for deductibles and consumables.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <a href="javascript:;" class="read-more-link">Read more</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
<!-- 21-04-2026 -->
  <section class="section-content read-more-option flex-wrap bg-sec-blue owl-div" id="optional-add-ons">
    <div class="il-container">
      <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What are the Key Add-ons Available in Bike Insurance?</h2>
      <p class="sub-txt   align-center">Here are some add-ons you can add to your two-wheeler insurance policy from ICICI Lombard, along with their benefits.</p>
      <div class="row-block mt-20 owl-grad owl-carousel owl-theme col-wrap">
        <div class="row-item">
          <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/il_smart_assist.webp" alt="IL Smart Assist" title="IL Smart Assist" class="lazy" width="50"></div>
          <div class="row-cont">
            <h3 class="heading3">IL Smart Assist</h3>
            <p class="text mt-10">This add-on is specially designed to offer enhanced on-road support and convenience services. Some of the key services include towing, battery jumpstart, flat tyre replacement, etc.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row-item">
          <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/roadside_assistance.webp" alt="Roadside Assistance" title="Roadside Assistance" class="lazy" width="50"></div>
          <div class="row-cont">
            <h3 class="heading3">Roadside Assistance</h3>
            <p class="text mt-10">This cover lets you stay ahead of unexpected breakdowns or accidents by offering 24/7 support. Be it breakdowns, key arrangement or minor repairs, the <a href="/motor-insurance/two-wheeler-insurance/roadside-assistance-cover" class="link" target="_blank">roadside assistance cover </a> ensures you’re never stranded.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row-item">
          <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/zero_depreciation.webp" alt="Zero Depreciation" title="Zero Depreciation" class="lazy" width="50"></div>
          <div class="row-cont">
            <h3 class="heading3">Zero Depreciation</h3>
            <p class="text mt-10">With this cover, you get the maximum claim amount without any deductions for depreciation on your bike’s parts. The  <a href="/motor-insurance/two-wheeler-insurance/blogs/what-is-zero-depreciation-in-bike-insurance" target="_blank" class="link">zero depreciation cover in bike</a>  applies only if your claim is for loss or damage to the vehicle.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row-item">
          <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/engine_protect_plus.webp" alt="Engine Protect Plus" title="Engine Protect Plus" class="lazy" width="50"></div>
          <div class="row-cont">
            <h3 class="heading3">Engine Protect Plus </h3>
            <p class="text mt-10">This add-on protects your bike’s engine parts and gearbox parts against damages caused due to water ingress or oil leakage. It will not cover added damage caused by delayed intimation or late removal from a waterlogged area.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row-item">
          <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/key_protect.webp" alt="Key Protect" title="Key Protect" class="lazy" width="50"></div>
          <div class="row-cont">
            <h3 class="heading3">Key Protect</h3>
            <p class="text mt-10">Get coverage for repairing or replacing your bike’s keys, locks and locksets as per your bike insurance policy’s terms and conditions. This add-on also covers the locksmith charges in case your key is stolen, misplaced or accidentally damaged.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row-item ">
          <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/garage_cash.webp" alt="Garage Cash " title="Garage Cash " class="lazy" width="50"></div>
          <div class="row-cont">
            <h3 class="heading3">Garage Cash </h3>
            <p class="text mt-10">Under this add-on, you get daily allowance if your bike is under repair at a garage for a specified number of days. You may also get a lump-sum amount if your bike is declared as total loss/constructive total loss/cash loss.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!-- <div class="row-item more-option-show">
          <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/health-revamp/power-booster.webp" alt="Power Booster" title="Power Booster"></div>
          <div class="row-cont">
            <h3 class="heading3">NCB Protect</h3>
            <p class="text mt-10">This add-on allows you to retain a significant portion of your No Claim Bonus (NCB) even after making a claim during the policy year. Note that you will lose all your NCB if you lodge more than three claims during a policy year.   </p>
          </div>
        </div> -->
        <div class="row-item more-option-show">
          <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/return_to_invoice.webp" alt="Return to Invoice" title="Return to Invoice" class="lazy" width="50"></div>
          <div class="row-cont">
            <h3 class="heading3">Return to Invoice</h3>
            <p class="text mt-10">In case of total loss, this add-on will help you bridge the gap between your bike’s IDV and the actual cost of buying a new bike of the same make and model. </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row-item more-option-show">
          <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/tyre_and_wheel_rim_protect.webp" alt="Tyre and Wheel RIM Protect " title="Tyre and Wheel RIM Protect " class="lazy" width="50"></div>
          <div class="row-cont">
            <h3 class="heading3">Tyre and Wheel RIM Protect </h3>
            <p class="text mt-10">It covers the cost of repairing or replacing tyres/tubes/ wheel rims if they are damaged due to an incident. It provides coverage in multiple situations, including sidewall indentations caused by an external impact.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row-item more-option-show">
          <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/consumables_cover.webp" alt="Consumables Cover" title="Consumables Cover" class="lazy" width="50"></div>
          <div class="row-cont">
            <h3 class="heading3">Consumables Cover</h3>
            <p class="text mt-10">It covers the cost of consumable items used during your bike repair/replacement process. Consumables include washers, brake oil, nut and bolt, lubricant, clip, screw, engine oil, oil filter, bearings, grease, fuel filter, coolant, etc.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      
      
      </div>
      <p class="note-txt">Note: Kindly go through the  <a href="https://www.icicilombard.com/downloads" class="link" target="_blank">policy wordings</a> for detailed information about different two-wheeler add-ons offered by ICICI Lombard. You can check the complete list of add-on covers in this <a href="/docs/default-source/default-document-library/two-wheeler-products-add-on-and-uin.pdf" class="link" target="_blank">document</a>.</p>
      <a href="javascript:;" class="read-more-opt-btn hide-in-mobile">Read more</a>
      
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-content " id="zero-deprecation-tw">
    <div class="il-container">
      <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What is Zero Depreciation in Bike Insurance?</h2>
      <p class="sub-txt width-90 mt-20 align-center">Zero Depreciation (also called Nil Depreciation) is an add‑on cover that helps you avoid the depreciation deduction applied on your bike or scooter’s parts during a claim. Under a standard policy, depreciation is applied based on the part type, for example, plastic, fibre, rubber, tyres, tubes and batteries attract higher depreciation compared to metal parts. Zero Depreciation helps ensure that the claim amount for replaced parts is calculated without factoring in depreciation, as per policy terms.</p>

      <p class="sub-txt width-90 mt-15 align-center strong-txt">Your bike depreciation also depends on its age. Here’s a breakdown of the same: </p>
      <div class="table-wrapper table-style1  width-85 mt-30">
        <table class="table-wrap">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th style="width: 50%">Bike Age</th>
              <th style="width: 50%">Percentage of Depreciation</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt" style="width: 50%">Less than 6 months</td>
              <td style="width: 50%">0%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt" style="width: 50%">More than 6 months but less than 1 year</td>
              <td style="width: 50%">5%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">More than 1 year but less than 2 years</td>
              <td>10%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">More than 2 years but less than 3 years</td>
              <td>15%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">More than 3 years but less than 4 years</td>
              <td>25%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">More than 4 years but less than 5 years</td>
              <td>35%</td>
            </tr>
             <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">More than 5 years but less than 10 years</td>
              <td>40%</td>
            </tr>
             <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">More than 10 years</td>
              <td>50%</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="width-90">
       <p class="align-center mt-20 sub-txt">Our zero depreciation add-on is ideal for people who have recently purchased a new bike, own a luxury two-wheeler, stay in metro cities or accident-prone areas, and looking for stronger financial protection. Note that this add-on is available at nominal extra premium.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-content bg-warmgray" id="idv-in-tw">
    <div class="il-container">
      <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What is IDV in Bike Insurance? </h2>
      <p class="sub-txt width-90 align-center">IDV (Insured Declared Value) is the maximum claim amount you may receive if your bike is stolen or suffers total loss (damage beyond repair), as per policy terms and conditions. It reflects your bike’s current market value after factoring in depreciation. </p>
      <p class="sub-txt width-90 align-center">In simple words, IDV is the amount you are likely to get if your bike is completely lost or destroyed. </p>

       <h3 class="heading3 align-center">How is IDV Calculated? </h3>
      <p class="align-center width-90 text sub-txt">
IDV is generally derived from: 
Ex‑showroom price – Depreciation (as applicable). 
As your bike gets older, depreciation increases, resulting in a lower IDV. </p>


       <h3 class="heading3 align-center">Illustrative Example: </h3>
      <p class="align-center width-90 text sub-txt">If your bike’s ex‑showroom price is ₹120,000, its IDV after one year may be around ₹102,000–₹100,000, depending on the applicable depreciation rate.</p>
      <p class="align-center width-90 text sub-txt"><em>(Values are only illustrative; actual IDV is determined as per policy guidelines.)</em></p>
       
       <p class="sub-txt width-90 mt-20 align-center strong-txt">Here’s the depreciation schedule for fixing your bike’s IDV:</p>
      <div class="table-wrapper table-style1  width-equal width-85 mt-30">
        <table class="table-wrap">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th style="width: 60%">Bike Age</th>
              <th style="width: 40%">% of Depreciation For Fixing IDV</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt" style="width: 50%">Not exceeding 6 months</td>
              <td style="width: 50%">5%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">Exceeding 6 months but not exceeding 1 year</td>
              <td>15%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">Exceeding 1 year but not exceeding 2 years</td>
              <td>20%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">Exceeding 2 years but not exceeding 3 years</td>
              <td>30%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">Exceeding 3 years but not exceeding 4 years</td>
              <td>40%</td>
            </tr>
             <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">Exceeding 4 years but not exceeding 5 years</td>
              <td>50%</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="note-txt">
       <p class="align-center mt-20 sub-txt">Note that IDV for bikes aged over five years and obsolete models is calculated based on mutual understanding between the insurer and the insured.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-content  owl-div bg-pink" id="factor-impact-idv">
    <div class="il-container">
      <h2 class="heading2 align-center">Which Factors Impact the IDV?</h2>
      <p class="sub-txt width-90 align-center">The Insured Declared Value (IDV) of your bike is influenced by a few key factors. These help determine the bike’s current market value for insurance purposes, as per policy terms.</p>
     
      <div class="col-wrap owl-carousel owl-theme owl-sec mt-30">
        <div class="col-item">
          <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/individual_health_insurances.webp" alt="Bike Insurance IDV Factor - Age of the Bike" title="Bike IDV Factor - Age of the Bike" class="lazy" width="290">
          <div class="col-content factor-impact">
            <h3 class="heading3">Age of the Bike</h3>
            <p class="text color-coolgray mt-10">IDV reduces as the bike gets older because depreciation increases with time. Older bikes naturally have a lower IDV.</p>
            
         
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-item">
          <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/bike_s_market_values.webp" alt="Bike’s Market Value" title="Bike’s Market Value" class="lazy" width="290">
          <div class="col-content factor-impact">
            <h3 class="heading3 ">Bike’s Market Value </h3>
            <p class="text color-coolgray mt-10">The make, model, and variant directly affect your bike’s market price. Premium models or bikes with higher demand usually have a higher IDV compared to regular models.</p>
          
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-item">
          <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/modifications_dones.webp" alt="	Modifications Done" class="lazy" title="	Modifications Done" width="290">
          <div class="col-content factor-impact">
            <h3 class="heading3">Modifications &amp; Accessories</h3>
            <p class="text color-coolgray mt-10">Any approved, listed accessories or modifications can influence IDV. These need to be declared in the policy to be considered in the IDV calculation. </p>
           
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-item">
          <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-tw-revamp/depreciation-rates.webp" alt="	Depreciation Rates " title="	Depreciation Rates " class="lazy" width="290">
          <div class="col-content factor-impact">
            <h3 class="heading3">	Depreciation Rates </h3>
            <p class="text color-coolgray mt-10">Depreciation is applied each year based on standard rates. Higher depreciation lowers the IDV as the bike ages.</p>
           
          </div>
        </div>
       
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-content" id="What-is-NCB-in-tw">
    <div class="il-container">
      <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What is NCB in Bike Insurance?</h2>
      <p class="sub-txt width-90 align-center">NCB (No Claim Bonus) is a benefit you earn from your insurer for completing a policy year without making any claims, as per policy terms and conditions. <br>
It offers a discount on the Own Damage premium at the time of renewal for every claim-free year. <br>

You can easily apply your NCB while renewing your bike insurance policy, provided there is no break in coverage and no claims were made in the previous term.  </p>
      <p class="sub-txt width-90 mt-20 align-center strong-txt">Here are the different NCB slabs for two-wheelers:</p>
      <div class="table-wrapper table-style1  width-80 mt-30">
        <table class="table-wrap">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th style="width: 50%">Scenario</th>
              <th style="width: 50%">Discount Percentage (Applicable Only on Own Damage Premium)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt" style="width: 50%">No claims in the first year </td>
              <td style="width: 50%">20%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">No claims in two consecutive years</td>
              <td>25%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">No claims in three consecutive years</td>
              <td>35%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">No claims in four consecutive years</td>
              <td>45%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="strong-txt">No claims in five consecutive years</td>
              <td>50%</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="width-90">
        <p class="align-center mt-20  sub-txt">As highlighted above, NCB offers discount on the own damage component of your bike insurance premium. Let’s understand this with an example. Suppose your own damage premium is ₹4000 and you have an NCB of 25%. Your NCB discount amount will be ₹1000, which is 25% of ₹4000. Note that NCB is not applicable on third-party premiums.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-content owl-div bg-sec-blue" id="Which-Factors-Affect-Tw-Premium">
    <div class="il-container read-more-option">
      <h2 class="heading2 align-center">Which Factors Affect Two-Wheeler Insurance Premium?</h2>
      <div class="option-block owl-block owl-carousel owl-theme col-wrap">
        <div class="option-item">
          <h3 class="heading3">Policy Type </h3>
          <p class="text">The type of policy you choose directly affects your premium. While third-party insurance is quite affordable, an own damage or comprehensive bike insurance offers wider protection.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="option-item">
          <h3 class="heading3">Engine’s Cubic Capacity </h3>
          <p class="text">Your bike insurance premium depends on your vehicle’s cubic capacity (CC). A higher CC model usually has a higher premium and vice versa.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="option-item">
          <h3 class="heading3">Bike’s Age &amp; Model </h3>
          <p class="text">Newer and premium bike models usually have higher IDV, which increases the premium. As your bike ages, its IDV lowers and the premium may depend on its condition and resale value.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="option-item more-option-show">
          <h3 class="heading3">Bike Modifications </h3>
          <p class="text">Any modifications that alter the bike’s performance or appearance can increase the IDV and impact the calculation of your bike insurance premium.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="option-item more-option-show">
          <h3 class="heading3">	No Claim Bonus (NCB)</h3>
          <p class="text">While frequent claims can lead to higher premiums, you earn a NCB discount for riding safely and not making a claim during a policy year. </p>
        </div>
        <div class="option-item more-option-show">
          <h3 class="heading3">Add-ons </h3>
          <p class="text">Opting for optional covers such as zero depreciation, engine protect, or roadside assistance increase your premium but also enhance bike insurance coverage.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
         <!-- <a href="javascript:;" class="read-more-opt-btn">Read more</a> -->
    </div>
  </section>

