  <section class="section-content bg-sec-blue" id="Choose-the-Right-tw">
    <div class="il-container">
      <div class="mid-width width-90">
        <h2 class="heading2 ">How to Choose the Right Two-wheeler Insurance Policy?</h2>
        <p class="text width-90">Buying bike insurance is not just about meeting a requirement. It is about choosing the right level of protection for how you ride. Here’s how to make a decision that works for you: </p>
        <div class="list-block org-list org-list-block mt-20">
          <ul>
            <li>
              <h4 class="heading4">	Start with your usage: </h4>
              <p class="text">Think about how often and where you use your bike. If your daily exposure is high, a comprehensive plan with add-ons will give you better protection than a basic third-party cover. </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h4 class="heading4">	Compare before you decide:</h4>
              <p class="text">Don’t pick a plan based on price alone. Look at what you are getting. Compare IDV, add-ons, deductibles, and benefits like No Claim Bonus (NCB). Choose what gives you the best overall value. </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h4 class="heading4">	Know what’s covered:</h4>
              <p class="text">Take a few minutes to check inclusions and exclusions. This helps you avoid surprises when you actually need to claim.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h4 class="heading4">Check how claims work:  </h4>
              <p class="text">A good plan should be easy to use when it matters. Look for a wide cashless garage network, simple digital claims, and quick approvals.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <a href="#" class="calculate-primium-btn primary-btn">Calculate Premium Now </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

