    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, you can buy bike insurance online for a second-hand bike after transferring ownership in your name."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can I insure a bike registered in another state?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, you can but inform the insurance company about the registration details and usage location."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is bike insurance required if the bike is not in use?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, you need at least a third-party bike insurance even if the bike is not in use."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can bike insurance be in someone else's name?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "No, the bike insurance policy should be in the registered owner’s name."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "How to check bike insurance status?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You can check details about your bike insurance online via your insurer website, policy document or the VAHAN portal using registration number."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is bike insurance transferable when ownership changes?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, it is."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What happens if I ride someone else’s bike and meet with an accident?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "It depends on your coverage type and whether you have a valid bike insurance policy at the time of the accident."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "How is the Insured Declared Value (IDV) of my vehicle decided and how does it impact my coverage?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "The IDV is based on your bike’s current market value after depreciation. It determines the maximum payout in case of total loss or theft."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Does bike insurance cover damages due to floods or cyclones?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, own damage bike insurance and comprehensive bike insurance covers damages due to floods or cyclones."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Are accidents caused due to drunk driving covered?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "No. Bike insurance does not cover accidents caused due to riding under the influence of alcohol or drugs."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Does bike insurance cover damages due to wear and tear?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "No, bike insurance does not cover damages arising from normal wear and tear."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is engine damage due to water ingress covered?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Bike insurance covers engine damage due to water ingress only if you have the Engine Protect Plus add-on."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Does bike insurance cover accidents outside my city or state?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, it does."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Are tyres and tubes covered under bike insurance?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, if your bike tyres and/or tubes were damaged in an accident (subject to depreciation)."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Are damages caused during racing or stunts covered?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "No, bike insurance does not cover damages caused during racing or stunts."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What are the turnaround times (TAT) for my insurance services?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Policy issuance is usually instant. However, the claims TAT depend on survey assessment, documents submitted and policy terms and conditions."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "In case I change my job and location, what happens to my bike insurance policy?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Your bike insurance policy remains valid, no matter where you shift in the country. Just inform us if you permanently move to another city or RTO zone."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can I have more than one bike insurance policy for the same bike?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "No, you cannot have two bike insurance policies with the same coverage type for one bike at the same time."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "How is motor insurance premium calculated?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Your bike insurance premium is calculated based on your vehicle’s IDV, age, engine CC, location, NCB and add-ons."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Does the bike insurance premium increase every year?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Your bike insurance premium may change due to IDV reduction, claim history or regulatory revisions."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Does installing an anti-theft device reduce premium?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, you get a discount on your bike insurance premium for installing approved anti-theft devices."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is GST included in bike insurance premium?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, an 18% GST is currently applicable on bike insurance premium."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Does modifying the bike increase premium?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, certain bike modifications can increase your bike insurance premium."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is a third-party bike insurance cheaper than comprehensive insurance?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, but it offers limited coverage compared to a comprehensive bike insurance."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is FIR mandatory for all bike insurance claims?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "An FIR is mandatory for claims related to theft and major third-party injuries/damages."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can I file an insurance claim for minor scratches or dents?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, you can but it may affect your NCB."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is there a time window for filing a claim?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "It is advisable to file a bike insurance claim as soon as possible after the incident."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can I track my bike insurance claim status online?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You can track the status of your bike insurance claim online via our website or IL TakeCare App or WhatsApp: 7738282666."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can I claim insurance if repairs are done outside network garage?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, you can file for a reimbursement. Just follow the details mentioned on our bike insurance claims page."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "How many claims can I make in a year?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Typically, you can file multiple claims but frequent claims can affect your NCB and claim history."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What happens to my NCB after a claim?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Your NCB resets to zero if you make a bike insurance claim unless you have the NCB Protect add-on."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What criteria is considered to classify my insured vehicle as a Total Loss, Constructive Total Loss, or Cash Loss?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "An insurer considers a vehicle as Constructive Total Loss when the total cost of repair or retrieval exceeds 75% of the bike’s IDV. Meanwhile, Total Loss applies when damage is beyond repair while Cash Loss refers to a negotiated settlement."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What happens if I miss my bike insurance renewal date?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Your bike insurance policy may lapse, and your bike may be required to undergo inspection before coverage is reinstated."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is there a grace period for the bike insurance renewal?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "It depends on the insurance company."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can I renew bike insurance after a long lapse?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, you can renew your bike insurance after a policy lapse subject to inspection and underwriting approval."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is vehicle inspection required after policy expiry?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, some insurers may require vehicle inspection after bike insurance expiry/lapse."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Will I lose NCB if policy lapses?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, you will lose your accumulated NCB if you don’t renew your bike insurance policy on time."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can I switch insurer while renewing bike insurance?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, you can easily port your bike insurance policy to another insurer at the time of renewal."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can I upgrade coverage during renewal?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, you can modify your IDV and opt for add-ons for enhanced coverage during renewal."
    }
  }]
}
</script>

