<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "name": "How to Calculate Two-Wheeler Insurance Premium Online?",
  "description": "Your bike insurance premium is calculated using a digital premium calculator available on the insurer’s website. The premium depends on factors such as your bike’s age and model, engine’s cubic capacity, IDV, type of coverage and add-on selected, and registration location.",
  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Enter your two-wheeler details, including registration number."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Step 2",
      "text": "Choose the coverage and add-ons you want."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Step 3",
      "text": "You will know premiums instantly."
    }
  ]
}
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "name": "How to Save on Bike Insurance Premium?",
  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Compare Plans Online",
      "text": "Don’t settle for the first quote. Comparing different bike insurance plans online allows you to find the best coverage at an attractive price."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Choose Right IDV",
      "text": "Know your bike’s correct market value before selecting the Insured Declared Value (IDV). A lower IDV may reduce your premium."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Claim NCB",
      "text": "Being a responsible driver reduces the chances of making a claim and availing of the benefits of NCB in bike insurance. Use it to your advantage to save on premiums."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Opt for Voluntary Deductible",
      "text": "You can opt for a higher voluntary deductible to reduce your bike insurance premium."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Renew on Time",
      "text": "Renew your bike insurance online on time to avoid policy lapse and protect your accumulated NCB."
    }
  ]
}
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "name": "How to Effectively Compare Bike Insurance Premium?",
  "description": "Comparing bike insurance premiums online isn’t about choosing the lowest price. It’s about getting the right coverage at the right value.",
  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Compare Plans Online",
      "text": "The first step is comparing bike insurance plans online. A third-party coverage is cheaper, but a comprehensive bike insurance covers both third-party liabilities and own damage."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Check IDV",
      "text": "Pay special attention to IDVs offered across different bike insurance quotes. A lower IDV reduces premium but also lowers your claim payout in case of theft or total loss."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Review Coverage Details",
      "text": "Carefully go through the policy inclusions and exclusions to understand what’s covered and what’s not covered. Some policies may appear cheaper but offer limited benefits."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Evaluate Add-ons",
      "text": "There are multiple add-on options available in the market to improve your bike insurance coverage. However, they attract additional premium. Evaluate your needs and select the ones that actually add value to your coverage."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Compare Deductibles",
      "text": "Opting for a higher voluntary deductible lowers your payable premium but increases your out-of-pocket expense during a bike insurance claim."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Review Premium Break-Up",
      "text": "Your premium is made up of multiple components like your own damage premium, your third-party liability premium, add-on premium, personal accident coverage premium, etc. Review your premium break-up before selecting a policy."
    }
  ]
}
</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "name": "How to Choose the Right Two-wheeler Insurance Policy?",
  "description": "Choosing the best bike insurance plan isn’t just about buying what’s mandatory. It’s about protecting your bike in a way that suits your usage, budget and risk exposure.",
  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Assess Your Needs",
      "text": "Start by understanding how you want to use your bike. If your risk exposure is high, a comprehensive bike insurance policy with add-ons may be more appropriate than a basic third-party bike insurance plan."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Compare Policies Online",
      "text": "Take bike insurance quotes from multiple insurers. Look beyond just the premium and compare IDV options, add-ons, deductibles and discounts like No Claim Bonus (NCB). Select the plan that suits your needs the best."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Review Coverage",
      "text": "Check what is included and excluded in your bike insurance policy to avoid surprises later. You can go through the policy wordings to get detailed information about your policy inclusions and exclusions."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Check Claim Process",
      "text": "A hassle-free and transparent claim process is crucial. Look for insurers with a wide network of cashless garages and easy digital claim filing. Faster approvals and minimal paperwork can make a big difference during emergencies."
    }
  ]
}
</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "name": "How to Buy Two-Wheeler Insurance Online?",
  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Share Details",
      "text": "Enter your bike details, including registration number, and your contact details."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Choose Bike Insurance Plan",
      "text": "Select the type of coverage you want: Third-party bike insurance, Own damage bike insurance or Comprehensive bike insurance."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Select Add-ons",
      "text": "Choose different add-ons to enhance your own damage or comprehensive bike insurance coverage based on your needs."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Choose Policy Tenure",
      "text": "You also get the option to choose the tenure of your bike insurance policy. It ranges from one year to five years."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Review Premium",
      "text": "Review your premium breakup and pay the applicable amount online."
    }
  ]
}
</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "name": "How to Renew a Two-Wheeler Insurance Policy?",
  "description": "You can easily renew your bike insurance online in a few clicks. Renewing your bike insurance policy on time helps you avoid any lapse in coverage and protects your accumulated NCB benefits.",
  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Visit Our Website/App",
      "text": "Visit our website or log in to our IL TakeCare App and select the “Renew” option."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Enter Details",
      "text": "Fill in the required details, including your vehicle number, existing policy details, etc."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Review Coverage Details",
      "text": "Check your existing coverage, IDV and add-ons. Make changes if needed. Select NCB, if applicable."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Make Payment",
      "text": "Make the required payment online to renew your policy."
    }
  ]
}
</script>

